00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:05.980
In the wider world, EU Trade Commissioner Morosh Shefshevich is in Beijing. Euro news says,

00:04:05.980 --> 00:04:09.100
for two days of talks meant to rebalance trade with China.

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:13.440
The broadcaster called that trade ever more one-sided over the past decade.

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:17.320
EuroNews says he arrived with a deadline to reset the relationship,

00:04:17.660 --> 00:04:20.500
and that the October EU summit is only days away.

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:23.440
It casts the visit as high stakes for that reset.

00:04:24.120 --> 00:04:28.680
The case on both sides today is whether seven genetically modified crop approvals

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:31.880
should stand when member governments would not vote them through.

00:04:32.380 --> 00:04:35.140
The European Commission approved or renewed them anyway.

00:04:35.140 --> 00:04:41.280
The case for them is the one Brussels acted on, favorable reviews from the European Food Safety Authority.

00:04:41.900 --> 00:04:46.380
U Craig Agro Consult says the decisions came in June and September 2026,

00:04:46.980 --> 00:04:50.920
four soybean events and three corn events for food and for animal feed.

00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:54.880
That report says the wider list matters most to Europe's feed industry,

00:04:55.220 --> 00:04:57.760
which depends heavily on soy and corn from abroad.

00:04:58.420 --> 00:05:03.160
Fresh approvals and renewals widen which cargoes can come in to be processed and fed to animals.

00:05:03.160 --> 00:05:14.500
The Soyavins are MON 94637, GMB151 crossed with DAS44406-6, and MON 94313.

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:24.180
The new cornstack is DP202216 crossed with NK603 and DAS40278-9.

00:05:24.180 --> 00:05:34.300
Renewals cover CornNK603 crossed with T25, CornMOM87460, and soybeanMOM87705.

00:05:34.760 --> 00:05:39.360
Brussels moved only after capitals failed to assemble a qualified majority on either side

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:39.780
of the vote.

00:05:40.260 --> 00:05:45.120
The case against, as those governments stated in the votes, is public hostility to genetically

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:49.900
modified crops, the precautionary principle, scientific doubts, and politics.

00:05:50.460 --> 00:05:52.660
They could not muster the votes to block the files.

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:55.360
They also could not muster the votes to pass them.

00:05:55.840 --> 00:05:57.500
What the paperwork itself locks in,

00:05:57.660 --> 00:05:59.320
which every way you read the politics,

00:05:59.720 --> 00:06:00.740
